1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:04,905
Israel's prime minister
received Washington's 72-hour

2
00:00:04,945 --> 00:00:08,581
proposal as a notification,
not a consultation.

3
00:00:08,621 --> 00:00:10,848
He knew the difference well —

4
00:00:10,888 --> 00:00:16,944
and this notification meant Israel had
been left out of the Islamabad channel.

5
00:00:16,984 --> 00:00:21,204
“Fordow is alive,” he told
his chief of staff. “It is.”

6
00:00:21,244 --> 00:00:23,836
“Then our mission isn't finished.”

7
00:00:23,876 --> 00:00:24,843
That was all.

8
00:00:24,883 --> 00:00:29,621
The short sentence became an
official statement within hours:

9
00:00:29,661 --> 00:00:34,243
“Israel retains the right to
continue unilateral operations

10
00:00:34,283 --> 00:00:38,395
until Iran's nuclear capability
is fully eliminated.”

11
00:00:38,435 --> 00:00:40,795
The world read it as a warning.

12
00:00:40,835 --> 00:00:46,488
It wasn't a warning — it was the
announcement of a decision already made.
